   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thank you, Victor. You're verified. I checked order Q-7801 from Taqueria Luz.\n\n- The order was promised for 6:15 PM and handed over at 6:45 PM, so it was 30 minutes late.\n- A late delivery of 16 to 44 minutes qualifies for account credit equal to the delivery fee. Your delivery fee was $2.99.\n- An earlier support contact this evening (ticket TK-902) already gave you that $2.99 credit, and it's on your account now.\n\nThat credit is the full compensation for this delay. I can't add more, because the same problem can't be compensated twice. Late deliveries are also compensated with account credit only, not a refund to your card.\n\nIf anything else was wrong with the order, such as a missing or incorrect item, tell me and I'll look into it."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, so the $2.99 is the whole thing? It was really late though, like 30 minutes past when it was supposed to show up. Is there nothing else you can do?"
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Yes, the $2.99 is the full amount. I know a 30-minute delay is frustrating, Victor. Under our policy, an order that arrives 16 to 44 minutes late gets credit equal to the delivery fee. The bigger 20% credit starts at 45 minutes late. Your order was 30 minutes late, so the $2.99 credit is the most I can offer for the delay. I can't add goodwill credits or refunds beyond that.\n\nI can still help if something was missing or wrong with your order. If you'd like to talk to a person about this, I can pass your case to a human specialist."
  },
